"""Build the requested evidence report from predeclared label-free plans and scoring."""
from common import *
plan=read(OUT/'plan.json');pur=read(OUT/'purity.json');batch=read(OUT/'batch_shifts.json')
assert sha(OUT/'plan.json')==pur['plan_sha256']
old=read(ROOT/'audit/calibrated/objective.json')['groups']['D448']['losses']
for kind in ['constant','random','cluster']:
 weighted=sum(r['slices']*r['fixed']['losses'][kind]['total'] for r in batch['batches'])/200
 assert abs(weighted-old[kind]['total'])<1e-7,(kind,weighted,old[kind]['total'])
out=[]
def put(x=''):out.append(x)
def table(headers,rows):
 put('| '+' | '.join(headers)+' |');put('| '+' | '.join(['---']*len(headers))+' |')
 for r in rows:put('| '+' | '.join(map(str,r))+' |')
 put()
def pct(x):return 'UNVERIFIED (no pairs)' if x is None else f'{100*x:.3f}'
put('# STEGO ideas: adjacent-slice positives and per-batch shifts\n')
put('Read-only diagnostics; no gradient training, no source or experiment edits, no dataset/cache/checkpoint changes, no installs/downloads. All new scripts and artifacts are confined to `audit/stego_ideas/`; CPU, two torch threads per process. These four validation patients informed earlier choices; this is not an untouched test.\n')
put('## Protocol and label-use ledger\n')
put('Task 1 plan producer: `pair_plan.py` → `plan.json`, affinity/coordinate arrays. It reads no annotation files and completes before `score.py` opens exactly 472 validation PNG masks from patients 5/6/8/30; `score.py` → `purity.json` produces every purity, label base rate, liver-anchor count and enrichment. Task 2 producer: `batch_shifts.py` → `batch_shifts.json`, with no labels. `report.py` renders these tables; access ledgers list all paths opened. No labels set shifts, select neighbors/coordinates or select examples.\n')
put('Features: existing `audit/improve/B2_448_features.npy`, 448 input, 28×28 grid, 768-D final-block normalized patch tokens, CLS removed and per-patch L2. No new backbone pass was necessary; prior replay provenance is `audit/preflight/extract_checks.json`. Affinity uses the imported sealed `ContrastiveCorrelationLoss.helper` including normalization and restored-global-mean centering (`experiments/stego_biomedclip/reference_loss.py:51`), recovered as negative returned loss for constant unit-cosine codes at shift zero. This is the same inversion used by SELECTIVITY; neither affinity nor centering is reimplemented. PAIRS `hard_labels` and `label_summary`, and SELECTIVITY `basic`, are AST-imported unchanged to avoid their unrelated runtime/output side effects; the two scorers are asserted to agree.\n')
put('Validation kNN: the old PAIRS validation cache describes 224-input features, so the 448 comparison uses the exact sealed 448 neighbor recipe from `experiments/stego_biomedclip/preflight.py:22`: L2-normalized image means, cosine, stable sorting, explicit self-exclusion, top seven of thirty. Validation-only diagnostic indices are saved under this output folder; existing caches are not modified. This is a deliberate resolution-specific neighbor recomputation, not an assumption that the old cache is a 448 cache.\n')
put('Spatial sampling follows PAIRS/SELECTIVITY: uniform 11×11 coordinates in [-1,1], the project bilinear `sample` with border padding/align_corners=True, and 2,048 fixed Cartesian positions of each 121×121 pair matrix for unrestricted pairs. Same-image uses the same coordinates on both sides, including self pairs; kNN enumerates every directed top-seven edge. Co-located pools keep all 121 diagonal pairs of a helper matrix computed using the same coordinates in both slices; this preserves the loss’s target-mean centering rather than centering only the diagonal. Random-patch baselines use the 2,048 Cartesian positions from those same slice edges and the same feature samples.\n')
put('Adjacent alignment: group by patient AND DICOM series UID, sort by physical position, then take both signs of offsets 1/2/3/5 (omit unavailable boundary neighbors). An identical normalized point in each saved per-slice square body-crop box is paired; native location is obtained by that box’s independent translation/scale. No flip, transpose, deformable/rigid registration, or label-based alignment. Patch labels use the same saved crop/padding, nearest resize to 448, then 16×16 occupancy >0.5 (ties background), and PAIRS nearest sampling at the feature coordinates. This is patch-majority purity, not native-pixel boundary accuracy.\n')
put('Matched rate definition: thresholds are set on all anchors separately in each eligible pair pool; liver-anchor rates are conditional and generally differ. Co-location alone has no score, so its budgeted rows use fixed-seed uniform sampling without replacement; co-location+affinity keeps the top 5/10/20% within the co-located pool, not 5/10/20% of all Cartesian cross-slice pairs. Unfiltered random baselines below give the expected purity for random thinning at every budget. Thresholds and sampling seeds are fixed before label reads.\n')
table(['Offset (both signs)','Directed slice edges','Unique anchors','Physical distance mm [min / median / max]'],[
 [key.replace('offset','±'),v['directed_edges'],v['anchor_slices'],' / '.join(f"{v['distance_mm'][k]:.4f}" for k in ['min','median','max'])] for key,v in plan['offset_info'].items()])
put('## Task 1: positive-source purity\n')
put('All percentages except overall attraction/retention use validation labels. In the liver-anchor subset, liver-target share = same-label rate = liver/liver rate, and mixed rate is its complement; this identity is used to avoid three duplicate columns. All-anchor target share also includes background→liver targets. `L-anchor N` reports selected liver-anchor draws, not independent slices/patients.\n')
table(['Source','Rate %','All: liver target %','All: same %','All: LL %','All: mixed %','L-anchor: target=same=LL %','L-anchor: mixed %','L-anchor N'],[
 [r['pool']+' '+r['source'],pct(r['attraction']),pct(r['liver_target_share_all']),pct(r['same_label']),pct(r['liver_liver']),pct(r['mixed']),pct(r['target_liver_given_anchor_liver']),pct(r['liver_anchors']['mixed']),r['anchor_liver_pairs']] for r in pur['rows']])
put('### Random/unfiltered baselines\n')
table(['Eligible pool','Pairs','All: liver target %','All: same %','All: LL %','All: mixed %','L-anchor: target=same=LL %','L-anchor: mixed %'],[
 [r['pool'],r['pairs'],pct(r['liver_target_share_all']),pct(r['same_label']),pct(r['liver_liver']),pct(r['mixed']),pct(r['target_liver_given_anchor_liver']),pct(r['liver_anchors']['mixed'])] for r in pur['baselines']])
put('The offset*_random rows randomize patch position within the same adjacent-image edges; offset* rows preserve co-location without affinity selection. Their difference isolates positional correspondence in the sampled pool. Same-image/kNN baselines randomize patches within their own image-edge pools, retaining their distinct image-pair sampling distributions.\n')
put('### Thresholds, conditional attraction and pair counts (reproducibility)\n')
put('The restored-mean affinity can exceed 1 because it is a shifted/centered cosine matrix, not a raw cosine; co-located cutoffs above 1 are therefore expected from the imported helper.\n')
table(['Source','Overall rate %','Affinity cutoff','Liver-anchor retained %','Selected pairs'],[
 [r['pool']+' '+r['source'],pct(r['attraction']),'uniform thinning' if r['threshold'] is None else f"{r['threshold']:.8f}",pct(r['attraction_liver_anchors']),r['pairs']] for r in pur['rows']])
put('## Task 2: self-calibrating shifts\n')
put('The exact PREFLIGHT 200-train-slice order, seed 20261003, saved positive-image choices, code construction and coordinate/permutation RNG are reused. There are twelve full batches of 16 and one final batch of 8; keeping that last batch includes all 200 slices without repetition. Each batch independently takes affinity quantiles 0.8/0.8/0.9; negative quantiles pool its five actual non-self batch permutations. Constant/random/one-hot K8 codes and all three losses use the imported objective, pinned weights 0.67/0.25/0.63, dropout disabled, no optimization. K8 assignments use the saved train-only seed-0 frozen-feature centers; no label mapping is used. Mean/SD below weight each batch equally (sample SD, ddof=1).\n')
table(['Term','Fixed D448','Per-batch mean ± SD','Min–max'],[
 [name,f"{batch['fixed'][i]:.8f}",f"{batch['mean'][i]:.8f} ± {batch['sd'][i]:.8f}",f"{batch['minimum'][i]:.8f}–{batch['maximum'][i]:.8f}"] for i,name in enumerate(['Intra','kNN','Random'])])
table(['Batch','Slices','Intra shift','kNN shift','Random shift','Constant loss','Random loss','K8 loss','Admissible'],[
 [r['batch'],r['slices'],*[f'{v:.6f}' for v in r['adaptive']['shifts']],*[f"{r['adaptive']['losses'][k]['total']:.8f}" for k in ['constant','random','cluster']],r['adaptive']['admissible']] for r in batch['batches']])
put('Each adaptive batch reaches 20%/20%/10% attraction to floating-point quantile precision; exact fractions and all unweighted component losses are in `batch_shifts.json`. Admissibility is constant loss > random loss AND K8 loss < random loss (lower loss is better).\n')
table(['Calibration','Admissible batches','Fraction'],[[name,f"{batch['passes'][name]}/13",pct(batch['passes'][name]/13)+'%'] for name in ['adaptive','fixed']])
table(['Batch','Fixed constant loss','Fixed random loss','Fixed K8 loss','Fixed intra/kNN/random attraction %'],[
 [r['batch'],*[f"{r['fixed']['losses'][k]['total']:.8f}" for k in ['constant','random','cluster']],' / '.join(pct(v) for v in r['fixed']['attraction'])] for r in batch['batches']])
put('The slice-weighted fixed-loss totals reproduce `audit/calibrated/objective.json` to <1e-7, asserted by `report.py`. No evidence here that per-batch calibration improves admissibility over fixed D448: both pass every sampled batch.\n')
def row(pool,source,rate):return next(r for r in pur['rows'] if r['pool']==pool and r['source']==source and r['rate']==rate)
a=row('offset1','colocated-only',.1);c=row('offset1','colocated+affinity',.1);f=row('same-image','affinity',.1);k=row('knn','affinity',.1)
put('## Verdict and UNVERIFIED\n')
put(f"Co-located adjacent-slice pairs have higher liver-target purity in these validation diagnostics: at 10% overall retention, ±1 gives {pct(a['target_liver_given_anchor_liver'])}% versus {pct(f['target_liver_given_anchor_liver'])}% same-image affinity and {pct(k['target_liver_given_anchor_liver'])}% kNN affinity, gains of {100*(a['target_liver_given_anchor_liver']-f['target_liver_given_anchor_liver']):.3f} and {100*(a['target_liver_given_anchor_liver']-k['target_liver_given_anchor_liver']):.3f} percentage points; affinity-filtered ±1 gives {pct(c['target_liver_given_anchor_liver'])}%. This supports higher pair purity, not improved learned segmentation.\n")
put('Batch variation is modest on this sample: SD 0.00612 intra, 0.00588 kNN and 0.00987 random, close to the fixed D448 values; adaptive and fixed shifts both pass 13/13 sampled batches. UNVERIFIED: dropout-on calibration, gradient contributions and optimization stability, benefit of either idea to liver segmentation, generalization to other cohorts, and patient-bootstrap uncertainty. High purity can result from local anatomical continuity and does not establish semantic discrimination between organs; tiny structures and boundaries are reduced by patch-majority labeling. Body-box alignment is not anatomical registration. Small selected liver-anchor counts at strict cutoffs and correlated slices limit precision of the percentages. These four patients informed earlier choices.\n')
put('Commands:\n```sh\npython3 -B audit/stego_ideas/pair_plan.py\npython3 -B audit/stego_ideas/batch_shifts.py\npython3 -B audit/stego_ideas/score.py\npython3 -B audit/stego_ideas/report.py\n```\n')
put(f"Runtimes: pair plan {plan['seconds']:.3f}s; label scoring {pur['seconds']:.3f}s; batch calibration {batch['seconds']:.3f}s. Plan SHA256 `{pur['plan_sha256']}`. All label-use claims are supported by `pair_plan_access.json`, `score_access.json`, `batch_access.json`; source hashes in `plan.json`.\n")
(OUT/'IDEAS.md').write_text('\n'.join(out)+'\n');ledger('report_access.json')
dump('verification.json',dict(fixed_objective_reproduced=True,tolerance=1e-7,plan_sha256=sha(OUT/'plan.json'),labels_only_validation_png=len(pur['label_paths'])==472,script='report.py',scripts_sha256={p.name:sha(p) for p in OUT.glob('*.py')}))
